From: Zaurus OS
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: pxa2xx-pcm: guard close() against a missing dmaengine runtime

close() can run on a substream that never got a dmaengine runtime: open()
returns 0 without calling snd_dmaengine_pcm_open() when the DAI has no
dma_params, and close can run twice per substream anyway (see the
pxa2xx-i2s patch) because snd_dmaengine_pcm_close_release_chan() kfree()s
prtd without clearing private_data.

Either way it frees something it shouldn't and corrupts the slab, which
zeroed a snd_monitor_file's list.next and made the next close of any sound
fd fault in snd_card_file_remove() - recursive fault, unkillable task.
---
--- a/sound/arm/pxa2xx-pcm-lib.c
+++ b/sound/arm/pxa2xx-pcm-lib.c
@@ -127,7 +127,19 @@
 
 int pxa2xx_pcm_close(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream)
 {
-	return snd_dmaengine_pcm_close_release_chan(substream);
+	int ret;
+
+	/* no runtime data means open() bailed early or we're being closed
+	 * twice. either way freeing it again trashes the slab. */
+	if (!substream->runtime || !substream->runtime->private_data)
+		return 0;
+
+	ret = snd_dmaengine_pcm_close_release_chan(substream);
+
+	/* it kfree()s prtd but leaves the pointer set */
+	substream->runtime->private_data = NULL;
+
+	return ret;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(pxa2xx_pcm_close);
 
